 "recipe": "(the same code ships in workbench/verify.py, so users recompute it on their own install):\n  part hash   = SHA-256 over, for every file under the part's directory in byte-sorted relative POSIX path order (skipping\n                __pycache__, *.pyc, verdict-free runtime state), the UTF-8 path, a NUL, the file's own SHA-256 (32 bytes)\n                - files the download ships zstd-packed are hashed as their unpacked bytes (the PACK_MANIFEST sha256)\n  leaf        = SHA-256(UTF-8 \"oracle7-part:\" + name + \":\" + part hash hex)\n  root        = binary Merkle tree over the leaves in name order; a level with an odd count carries its last node up\n                unchanged; a parent is SHA-256(left || right) of the raw 32-byte digests\nParts: every specialist directory (specialists/<dir>), the specialists' gate tools, the admitted fold chain, the workbench,\nthe launcher. Stores are covered by PACK_MANIFEST.json, whose own hash is a part.",
